{
  "course": "初中60短文",
  "passage": 34,
  "title": "Passage 34",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 1,
      "sourceSentenceId": 1,
      "chunkId": "s34-p01",
      "image": "assets/images/01.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p01.mp3",
      "en": "The world's best athletes get together for the Olympic Games every four years.",
      "cn": "全世界的顶尖运动员每四年齐聚一堂，参加奥林匹克运动会。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 2,
      "sourceSentenceId": 2,
      "chunkId": "s34-p02",
      "image": "assets/images/02.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p02.mp3",
      "en": "The 2024 Olympic Games took place in Paris, France.",
      "cn": "2024年的奥运会在法国巴黎举行。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 3,
      "sourceSentenceId": 3,
      "chunkId": "s34-p03",
      "image": "assets/images/03.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p03.mp3",
      "en": "For the first time, people watched breaking as a new event at the Olympics.",
      "cn": "这一次，霹雳舞作为奥运会的一个新比赛项目首次亮相，让观众一饱眼福。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 4,
      "sourceSentenceId": 4,
      "chunkId": "s34-p04",
      "image": "assets/images/04.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p04.mp3",
      "en": "Breaking is also called break dancing.",
      "cn": "霹雳舞也被称为break dancing。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 5,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s34-p05",
      "image": "assets/images/05.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p05.mp3",
      "en": "It is popular among the youth today.",
      "cn": "它如今很受年轻人欢迎。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 6,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s34-p06",
      "image": "assets/images/06.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p06.mp3",
      "en": "The high-energy, skillful dance includes moves such as Top Rock, Footwork, Go Down, Freeze and so on.",
      "cn": "这种充满活力、技巧性强的舞蹈包括Top Rock、Footwork、Go Down、Freeze等动作。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 7,
      "sourceSentenceId": 7,
      "chunkId": "s34-p07",
      "image": "assets/images/07.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p07.mp3",
      "en": "The dancers need to think and show the moves of the hands and feet quickly.",
      "cn": "舞者需要快速思考并展示手脚的动作。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 8,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s34-p08",
      "image": "assets/images/08.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p08.mp3",
      "en": "Break dance battles are a common way to find out who is the best dancer.",
      "cn": "霹雳舞对决是找出最佳舞者的一种常见方式。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 9,
      "sourceSentenceId": 9,
      "chunkId": "s34-p09",
      "image": "assets/images/09.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p09.mp3",
      "en": "In the 1970s in New York City, fighting with others among teenage girls and boys became more and more serious.",
      "cn": "20世纪70年代，在纽约市，年轻男孩和女孩之间的斗殴变得越来越严重。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 10,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s34-p10",
      "image": "assets/images/10.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p10.mp3",
      "en": "Some of them began to deal with the problem through dance instead.",
      "cn": "其中一些人转而开始通过舞蹈解决这个问题。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 11,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s34-p11",
      "image": "assets/images/11.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p11.mp3",
      "en": "Just then, the dance style first showed up on the streets.",
      "cn": "就在那时，这种舞蹈风格首次出现在街头。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 12,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s34-p12-01",
      "image": "assets/images/12.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p12-01.mp3",
      "en": "In a \"battle\" like this, one dancer will show off his kicks and spins,",
      "cn": "在这样的“斗舞”中，一名舞者会展示踢腿和旋转动作，"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 13,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s34-p12-02",
      "image": "assets/images/12.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p12-02.mp3",
      "en": "and then the next will continue to compete.",
      "cn": "然后下一名舞者继续比拼。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 14,
      "sourceSentenceId": 13,
      "chunkId": "s34-p13",
      "image": "assets/images/13.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p13.mp3",
      "en": "Everyone keeps their spirits up.",
      "cn": "每个人都保持着高昂的情绪。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 15,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s34-p14",
      "image": "assets/images/14.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p14.mp3",
      "en": "The best dancer will finally be picked out and gain his grand victory.",
      "cn": "最后，最佳舞者会被选出并赢得胜利。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 16,
      "sourceSentenceId": 15,
      "chunkId": "s34-p15",
      "image": "assets/images/15.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p15.mp3",
      "en": "Today, there are battles held in a local hall, where dancers are scored and voted for based on their performance.",
      "cn": "如今，有些对决在当地礼堂举行，评委根据舞者的表现进行打分和投票。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 17,
      "sourceSentenceId": 16,
      "chunkId": "s34-p16-01",
      "image": "assets/images/16.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p16-01.mp3",
      "en": "The planners added breaking to the Olympics,",
      "cn": "奥运会组织者将霹雳舞列入比赛项目，"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 18,
      "sourceSentenceId": 16,
      "chunkId": "s34-p16-02",
      "image": "assets/images/16.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p16-02.mp3",
      "en": "because it meets the standard of being widely practised by men and women in a large number of countries.",
      "cn": "因为它符合在许多国家由男女广泛练习这一标准。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 19,
      "sourceSentenceId": 17,
      "chunkId": "s34-p17",
      "image": "assets/images/17.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p17.mp3",
      "en": "\"Breaking has been accepted as a sport. I really feel proud,\" said Xiaoyu, one breakdancer.",
      "cn": "“霹雳舞已经被认可为一项体育运动。我真的感到很自豪。”一位名叫小雨的霹雳舞者说道。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 20,
      "sourceSentenceId": 18,
      "chunkId": "s34-p18",
      "image": "assets/images/18.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s34-p18.mp3",
      "en": "\"And for the Olympics, it will get more attention from young people who may not follow some of the traditional sports.\"",
      "cn": "“而且对奥运会来说，它会吸引更多年轻人的关注，这些年轻人可能并不关注一些传统运动。”"
    }
  ],
